==Finnish==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|non|fi}} {{term|Eiríkr|lang=non}}. Brought to Finland as an {{etyl|gmq-osw|fi}} saint's name in the Middle Ages. Cognate to Swedish {{term|Erik|lang=sv}} and English {{term|Eric|lang=en}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|/ˈerik/|lang=fi}}
* {{hyphenation|E|rik}}

===Proper noun===
